1. Function gets memmory
When a function is called c++ creates a small temporary memory area called a stack frame to store :
parameters
local variables

2. Input (parameters) are copied into that memory.
if you call (3,5) the function receives :
a = 3 , b = 5

3. Function runs its statement
Inside the function it executes line by line

4. If there is a return value it sends it back.
when the function ends its temporary memory deletes.
